# The DEFAULT graph-sweep noise list — ccrc's own footprint, and nothing else.
#
# D-1160. `_gs_guard` refuses a build when any path `detect()` picks up is not
# git-tracked, because an untracked file entering the corpus would silently
# change a graph nobody can reproduce. That guard is right. What was wrong is
# that ccrc's OWN tooling writes untracked files into every repo a session
# touches — `.remember/` transcripts, `.superpowers/` specs, `.claude/`
# settings, a `CLAUDE.local.md` — and those files were then held against the
# repo, refusing its build for ever.
#
# Measured on the reference fleet before this list existed: 14 of 57 trees
# refused, 304 breach paths, of which 186 were these four. Five repos were
# blocked by NOTHING BUT ccrc's own artifacts.
#
# THE LINE THIS FILE DRAWS — and D-1161 is the deviation that made the line a
# MECHANISM instead of this paragraph. Only what ccrc and its skills create is
# noise. A repo's own files are not, and `.graphifyignore` cannot tell the
# difference: it is a pure path filter that knows nothing about git. So the
# sweep asks git instead — `git ls-files -c -i -X` names the TRACKED files a
# pattern would hide — and WITHHOLDS any pattern from this file that would hide
# tracked content, logging what it withheld. Seven repos on the reference fleet
# commit `.claude/` or `.superpowers/` content, three of them among the five
# this list was written to unblock; without the withholding rule the sweep
# dropped their tracked nodes from the corpus, graphify's shrink guard saw an
# unaccounted net loss and refused the write, and the tree wedged at
# `refused-shrink` on every pass — worse than the staleness being fixed.
#
# So a pattern here is advice that yields. A pattern in `<repo>.list` beside it
# is the operator's instruction about one repo and is honoured as written,
# tracked content included — that is the escape hatch, and it is the only one,
# because a '!' line anywhere refuses every build on the box.
#
# ccrc OWNS this file and rewrites it on install; operator additions belong in
# `<repo>.list`, which is unioned with this one.
.claude/
.remember/
.superpowers/
CLAUDE.local.md
